title: 'collectives-westend: deny value-moving calls to the `NonTransfer` proxy'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Applies the Collectives Polkadot fix from
    [fellows/runtimes#1341](https://github.com/polkadot-fellows/runtimes/pull/1341) to Collectives
    Westend: the `Fellowship`, `Ambassador` and `Secretary` proxies now admit only the
    `pallet_salary` calls that pay the claimant itself, omitting `payout_other`, which pays the
    claimant's salary to any account. `NonTransfer` also keeps denying `payout_other`, so only
    `Any` proxies can redirect salary payouts. Since the salary proxies no longer admit
    `payout_other`, `NonTransfer` remains a superset of `Fellowship`, `Ambassador` and (unlike on
    Collectives Polkadot, where `NonTransfer` is an allowlist that does not cover the Secretary
    calls) `Secretary`.

    Additionally, `NonTransfer` now denies `PolkadotXcm`, whose `transfer_assets`,
    `teleport_assets` and `execute` calls move assets to another chain.
crates:
- name: collectives-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
